 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in relation to filing of\nnotification to municipalities",
    "basePrintNo": "S6416",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6416-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §110-b, ABC L",
    "lawSection": "Alcoholic Beverage Control Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6416\n\nSPONSOR: SEPULVEDA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the alcoholic beverage control law, in\nrelation to filing of notification to municipalities\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis bill would provide that notifications that are required to be filed\nwith a municipality be filed no earlier than 270 days prior to the\nfiling of the application with the Authority.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill would amend ABCL § 110-b(1) to provide that\nnotifications that are required to be filed with a municipality be filed\nno earlier than 270 days prior to the filing of the application with the\nAuthority.\n\nSection 2 of the bill would make it take effect immediately and apply to\nany notification filed after it shall be signed into law.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCommunity Boards and other municipal governments have expressed\nconfusion by the notifications that liquor license applicants are statu-\ntorily required to forward to them, particularly when some license\napplicants currently send notification long before sending their actual\nlicense application to the Authority. This amendment would require\nlicense applicants to notify Community Boards and local municipalities\nno earlier than 270 days before filing their applicant with the Authori-\nty. This amendment would assist Community Boards and other municipal\ngovernments with their ability to provide their opinion for or against\nthe granting of such application, pursuant to ABCL 110-b.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATION:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
